+## Presenter design source
.trellis/spec/frontend/component-guidelines.md:24: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/component-guidelines.md:25: trailing whitespace.
+Root `DESIGN.md` defines the Claude-inspired FerroStage presenter theme. Task 07 creates the single `ui/src/theme.rs` token layer; 08 and 09 consume it. Use system fonts, explicit control states and visible keyboard focus. Never theme PDF/media pixels or pass settings/theme controllers to the audience snapshot. Source token contrast evidence does not establish native UI verification.
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:1: trailing whitespace.
+# Hook Guidelines
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:2: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:3: trailing whitespace.
+There are no React hooks, no `useEffect`, and no data-fetching hooks.
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:4: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:5: trailing whitespace.
+## What to do instead
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:6: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:7: trailing whitespace.
+GPUI will notify a view through its context (`cx.notify()` after a model update). Until that dependency exists, commands use `PresentationState::apply_at` with the app's monotonic clock sample:
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:8: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:9: trailing whitespace.
+```rust
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:10: trailing whitespace.
+presentation
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:11: trailing whitespace.
+    .apply_at(PresentationCommand::ToggleBlank(BlankMode::Black), now)?;
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:12: trailing whitespace.
+let snapshot = presentation.audience_snapshot();
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:13: trailing whitespace.
+```
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:14: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:15: trailing whitespace.
+Subscribe to the snapshot. Do not poll the filesystem from a view. Hot reload is `ferrostage-platform`'s job (300 ms debounce, validation, then a coordinated descriptor/document/visual commit). The temporary `StageShadowDocument` bridge does not implement that transaction.
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:16: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:17: trailing whitespace.
+## Forbidden
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:18: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:19: trailing whitespace.
+- A custom hook crate, a signals library, or `yew`/`leptos` patterns copied into GPUI code.
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:20: trailing whitespace.
+- `unsafe` view code to poke a window handle.
.trellis/spec/frontend/hook-guidelines.md:21: trailing whitespace.
+- Starting a thread inside a view. The render worker lives in `ferrostage-render` and is singular because PDFium is not parallel.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:1: trailing whitespace.
+# State Management
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:2: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:3: trailing whitespace.
+There is one presenter state and one audience projection.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:4: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:5: trailing whitespace.
+| State | Owner | Who may read it |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:6: trailing whitespace.
+|-------|--------|-----------------|
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:7: trailing whitespace.
+| `PresentationState` | `ferrostage-core` | Presenter commands via `apply_at(command, Instant)`; `elapsed_at` is pure and core never samples the clock |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:8: trailing whitespace.
+| `AudienceProjectionSnapshot` | Core metadata from `audience_snapshot`, matching visual added by the UI assembler | Audience window only while `Presenting`; the presenter may also read it. Includes `stage: AudienceStage`. `Idle` / `Ready` snapshots are `Curtain` and carry no visual |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:9: trailing whitespace.
+| `SlideNotes` | `ferrostage-document` | Presenter window only |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:10: trailing whitespace.
+| `Settings` | `ferrostage-settings` | App and presenter-side consumers. Successful runtime edits are saved; failed runtime application rolls back before save. A failed save keeps the runtime value and shows unsaved. A future `schema_version` is read-only and is not reset or written back |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:11: trailing whitespace.
+| `MonitorId` + `MonitorRole` | `display.monitors` | The only role authority. Not monitor indexes |
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:12: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:13: trailing whitespace.
+`SwapScreens` is an intent to the app role coordinator. One settings transaction exchanges the two `MonitorRole` bindings and moves the windows. It does not flip an authoritative swap flag, and it does not change `current_page` or `slide_crop`. Core has no swap flag. Direct `apply_at(SwapScreens, now)` returns `ScreenSwapRequiresCoordinator` without changing state; the app handles this intent before core dispatch.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:14: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:15: trailing whitespace.
+Core `AudienceProjectionSnapshot` includes `stage` and `visual`; its metadata projection always sets `visual=None`. Tasks 08/11 supply matching pixels. Task 02 source now contains a sectioned settings schema and `SettingsStore`; runtime UI application and save-status display remain task 09 work. The audience window is absent outside `Presenting`. A saved Audience that is missing does not fall back to another monitor (see the [frontend quality guidelines](./quality-guidelines.md)).
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:16: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:17: trailing whitespace.
+The audience view receives only the assembled snapshot, never the document, notes, media sources, a full-cache handle, or an arbitrary-page request API. The assembler publishes matching generation/page/crop/target pixels together; it keeps the previous complete projection until the next one is ready. `Curtain` and black/white blank cover every visual layer immediately.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:18: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:19: trailing whitespace.
+Blank mode is `Option<BlankMode>` on the snapshot so the audience window does not invent a second blank flag.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:20: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:21: trailing whitespace.
+## Forbidden
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:22: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:23: trailing whitespace.
+- A global `lazy_static` deck.
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:24: trailing whitespace.
+- Cloning speaker notes into the snapshot "just for the audience highlighter".
.trellis/spec/frontend/state-management.md:25: trailing whitespace.
+- Two copies of the current page index, one in the view and one in the core. The view sends a command and renders the snapshot it gets back.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:1: trailing whitespace.
+# Type Safety
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:2: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:3: trailing whitespace.
+Prefer newtypes over bare integers.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:4: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:5: trailing whitespace.
+```rust
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:6: trailing whitespace.
+pub struct DocumentGeneration(pub u64);
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:7: trailing whitespace.
+pub struct PhysicalPage(pub usize);
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:8: trailing whitespace.
+pub struct LogicalSlide(pub usize);
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:9: trailing whitespace.
+```
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:10: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:11: trailing whitespace.
+`DocumentGeneration` is ordered. A shadow load must pass a strictly greater value or `apply_at` returns `CoreError::StaleGeneration`.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:12: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:13: trailing whitespace.
+`NormalizedRect` is page space in the unit square. Use `FULL`, `LEFT_HALF`, `RIGHT_HALF`, `TOP_HALF`, and `BOTTOM_HALF` instead of repeating the numbers. `is_inside_unit_square` rejects non-finite or overflowing crops.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:14: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:15: trailing whitespace.
+`BlankMode` is an enum (`Black`, `White`). Do not pass a `bool` and a comment.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:16: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:17: trailing whitespace.
+## Notes boundary
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:18: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:19: trailing whitespace.
+`AudienceProjectionSnapshot` has no notes field. `LoadedDocument::project` accepts `Option<&SlideNotes>` and does not read it, so a test can prove the secret string never appears in the snapshot's `Debug` output.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:20: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:21: trailing whitespace.
+## Forbidden
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:22: trailing whitespace.
+
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:23: trailing whitespace.
+- `String` for a page index.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:24: trailing whitespace.
+- RGBA color tuples on the audience path. Stroke color is `[u8; 4]` BGRA.
.trellis/spec/frontend/type-safety.md:25: trailing whitespace.
+- `unsafe` transmute between `PhysicalPage` and `LogicalSlide`.
